.TH SDL_GetScancodeName 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetScancodeName \- Get a human-readable name for a scancode.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_keyboard.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetScancodeName(SDL_Scancode scancode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR Warning :
The returned name is by design not stable across platforms, e\[char46]g\[char46] the name for
.BR SDL_SCANCODE_LGUI
is \(dqLeft GUI\(dq under Linux but \(dqLeft Windows\(dq under Microsoft Windows, and some scancodes like
.BR SDL_SCANCODE_NONUSBACKSLASH
don\(aqt have any name at all\[char46] There are even scancodes that share names, e\[char46]g\[char46]
.BR SDL_SCANCODE_RETURN
and
.BR SDL_SCANCODE_RETURN2
(both called \(dqReturn\(dq)\[char46] This function is therefore unsuitable for creating a stable cross-platform two-way mapping between strings and scancodes\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I scancode
the desired
.BR SDL_Scancode
to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the name for the scancode\[char46] If the scancode doesn\(aqt have a name this function returns an empty string (\(dq\(dq)\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

